  "description": "Event Details Date: 23 October 2026 Time: 10:30 AM – 12:00 PM Venue: LAB 1, 2, 3, 4, I.T.S. Engineering College, Greater Noida Registration Fee: ₹300 per team Prize Pool: ₹15,000 Team Size: 4 participants per team Coordinator: Mr. Vidit Gaur Event Description BGMI – Battle Zone is a competitive gaming event at TechTrix'26, where teams compete against each other across multiple rounds and maps. The tournament focuses on teamwork, strategic decision-making, coordination, and competitive performance, with points earned through in-game eliminations and final ranking. This is a BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) event — high-speed Wi-Fi and snacks will be provided, but participants must bring their own mobile devices. Guidelines Team Size 4 participants per team Requirements Participants must bring their own mobile devices Only registered players are allowed to participate Participants must report before their scheduled match Tournament Format 2 rounds, played on different maps The team with the highest cumulative score across both rounds is declared the winner Map, server, and match settings will be fixed by the organizers, and the organizer's recorded result will be treated as official Genuine technical issues must be reported immediately to the referee/coordinator; a technical issue caused by a participant's own unauthorized software or settings will normally be treated as the participant's responsibility Judging Criteria Scoring is based on cumulative points across both rounds: Kills: 2 points each Rank Placement: 1 point Chicken Dinner: 10-point victory bonus The team with the highest cumulative score across the tournament rounds wins Disqualification The following are strictly prohibited and may result in disqualification: Account sharing Cheats, hacks, macros, or unauthorized scripts Exploiting known game bugs or glitches Deliberate disconnections or match manipulation Interference with another player's system or event infrastructure Abusive or threatening behaviour The",
