    "details": "<p><strong data-start=\"602\" data-end=\"624\">Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 23 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> 10:30 AM &ndash; 12:00 PM</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> LAB 1, 2, 3, 4, I.T.S. Engineering College, Greater Noida</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee:</strong> ₹300 per team</li>\n<li><strong>Prize Pool:</strong> ₹15,000</li>\n<li><strong>Team Size:</strong> 4 participants per team</li>\n<li><strong>Coordinator:</strong> Mr. Vidit Gaur</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Event Description</strong></p>\n<p>BGMI &ndash; Battle Zone is a competitive gaming event at TechTrix'26, where teams compete against each other across multiple rounds and maps. The tournament focuses on teamwork, strategic decision-making, coordination, and competitive performance, with points earned through in-game eliminations and final ranking. This is a BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) event &mdash; high-speed Wi-Fi and snacks will be provided, but participants must bring their own mobile devices.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Guidelines</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Team Size</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>4 participants per team</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Participants must bring their own mobile devices</li>\n<li>Only registered players are allowed to participate</li>\n<li>Participants must report before their scheduled match</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tournament Format</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>2 rounds, played on different maps</li>\n<li>The team with the highest cumulative score across both rounds is declared the winner</li>\n<li>Map, server, and match settings will be fixed by the organizers, and the organizer's recorded result will be treated as official</li>\n<li>Genuine technical issues must be reported immediately to the referee/coordinator; a technical issue caused by a participant's own unauthorized software or settings will normally be treated as the participant's responsibility</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Judging Criteria</strong></p>\n<p>Scoring is based on cumulative points across both rounds:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Kills:</strong> 2 points each</li>\n<li><strong>Rank Placement:</strong> 1 point</li>\n<li><strong>Chicken Dinner:</strong> 10-point victory bonus</li>\n<li>The team with the highest cumulative score across the tournament rounds wins</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Disqualification</strong></p>\n<p>The following are strictly prohibited and may result in disqualification:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Account sharing</li>\n<li>Cheats, hacks, macros, or unauthorized scripts</li>\n<li>Exploiting known game bugs or glitches</li>\n<li>Deliberate disconnections or match manipulation</li>\n<li>Interference with another player's system or event infrastructure</li>\n<li>Abusive or threatening behaviour</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Event Jury/Referee/Technical Committee holds final authority on match outcomes, penalties, and rule interpretation.</p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"602\" data-end=\"624\">NOTE-: Registration Fees are not refundable.</strong></p>",
